  "lineage": "Song and dance music of the Gurage, a Semitic-speaking people of the Gurage Zone south-west of Addis Ababa, around towns such as Wolkite and Butajira. Its fast group dances are driven by sung verses and intense hand-clapping, and the style reached a national audience through Guragigna songs recorded by Addis Ababa singers such as Mahmoud Ahmed.",
